WEBVTT

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.480
[December, Kyoto]

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.560
[Victory]
[Mitsuhoshi Bank]

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.160
[Ito Koji vs. Shiratori Mikoto]

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:21.520
I can still…!

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.300
I'm… fired?

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.280
We gave you a year.

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:30.380
A whole year.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.060
I can do better, I promise!

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.410
Well, if you insist, we better see some results
from you at the next tournament.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.960
Results are all that matters at Mitsuhoshi.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.840
If I can just win this rally, I can still…!

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.080
[March, Kyoto]

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:52.800
Loser.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.340
[Thank you for working with us.
- Mitsuhoshi Bank/Badminton Team]

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.440
[Mom]

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.050
Hey, Mikoto?
Why didn't you tell me you got fired?!

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.880
I just sent you a text about it.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.000
Oh, please!

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:30.340
If you're planning to come home,
I'm afraid your room isn't yours anymore.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:31.040
What?

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:32.760
An iguana?!

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:36.710
I mean, you suddenly go work
for a company in Kyoto…

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.780
I was sure you wouldn't be coming back!

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:40.380
Am I right, Mikey?

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.040
[Mik(ey)'s room]
Am I right, Mikey?

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.620
But I guess Mitsuhoshi doesn't go easy on anyone.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.900
To think that not even child prodigy Mikoto
was good enough for them…

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.040
Please don't call me that.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:55.960
Hey, if singles didn't work out for you,
why not go back to doubles?

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.120
Yeah, not happening.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.320
Anyway, I'm coming home for now.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.660
Oh, while you're in Kyoto,
could you get me some yatsuhas…?

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:12.540
Is this really it for me…?

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.620
Mom, not again…

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:23.620
Hello?

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:25.800
Yes, speaking.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.840
An offer? For me…?

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.620
[April, Urawa]

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.300
[April, Urawa]
The phone call on that fateful day

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:08.880
[#01: Assign]
was an offer from the coach of the team
from Sunlight Beverage.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.040
was an offer from the coach of the team
from Sunlight Beverage.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.660
My life as a badminton player wasn't over yet.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.780
So the park is a shortcut…?

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:21.120
[New message from Mom]

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.350
[Are you up? I got your suit cleaned]
How old do you think I am…

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:27.980
[Got your handkerchief? And your tie?]

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:34.210
Welcome.

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:45.820
Honestly, I'm here to play badminton.
Why do I have to get all dressed up?

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.220
Oh, just a drunk.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:05:59.960
Excuse me!

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:03.840
Water… please…

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:14.230
That hits the spot!

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.720
Right, I'll be off, then…

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.540
Now wait a second!

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:24.300
You're my savior!
I gotta thank you properly!

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.960
Oh no, don't worry about…

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:27.440
Wow, he reeks!

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:32.080
Aw, baby's first necktie.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:39.860
Plain knots are the standard for newbies
like you, but personally, I recommend…

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.840
Wait, I didn't ask for…!

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.820
Oh crap, I can't be late on my first day…!

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:48.200
Best of luck, new boy!

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:56.400
I made it…

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:01.000
This is Shiratori Mikoto, he will be a part
of our sales department starting today.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:07.260
If you ever have any questions or issues,
just ask one of us, okay?

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:12.220
Your tie!

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:18.250
Whoa, what is that?

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:23.600
Didn't you tie it yourself?

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:25.480
Are you here to party?

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.560
That asshole!

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:31.000
Good morning!

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:33.540
Tatsu, you're late!

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:35.540
Not another night course, was it?

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.280
Oh, you know, Waoko just wouldn't let me go!

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:40.320
What…

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.620
What are you doing here?!

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:44.860
Why hello, new boy.

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:46.860
How'd you like my tying technique?

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:49.440
Really took your breath away, huh?

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.240
Oh, you two know each other!
Great, that helps.

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:56.000
[Miyazumi Tatsuru, 32, SB Sales Dept.]
This is Miyazumi,
he's the king of sales around here.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.960
[Miyazumi Tatsuru, 32, SB Sales Dept.]
You'll be working with him.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.100
And while we're at it,
I'm also on the badminton team.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.500
Go easy on me, partner!

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:06.380
Huh?!

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:11.940
Sunlight Beverage has been
in the beverage business for 40 years now.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:14.700
Local sodas have been our main product,

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:16.870
and ten years ago, we added craft beer…

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:19.000
Are you even listening?

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:20.260
Natto cola…

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:23.160
Yeah, I don't know how
that one got so big either.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:27.800
Um, don't we need to go to practice…?

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:31.620
Rejoice! We're almost done making the rounds.

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.100
Good morning!

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:38.780
Here's the new kid who joined us today.
Hope you'll help him settle in.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:45.160
I'm Shiratori Mikoto.
Excited to meet everyone.

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:46.260
Mikoto?!

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.340
You're the new guy?!

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:49.080
Toya?

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:50.680
You know each other?

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:53.380
[Saeki Toya, 19, SB Planning Dept.]
We were on the same team back in high school.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.460
[Saeki Toya, 19, SB Planning Dept.]
He's a real heel though!

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:58.480
He moved to Kyoto
without as much as a peep to his buddies.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:00.400
Sorry…

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:03.100
Yeah? Then why do I
get the feeling you're not sorry at all?

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:06.350
You should've told us you were back,
I thought we were friends.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:08.080
Or is it that…

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:11.500
You still haven't gotten over
what happened at the Interhigh?

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.940
No, why would you think that?

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.360
Wow, would you look at the time.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:20.900
So we can go pract…

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:22.640
Time for the rounds outside the company!

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.900
What?! You said we were almost done.

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:27.260
Within the company, that is.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:29.440
Practice starts at 4pm.

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:38.240
Boy, have I got a lot to teach you!

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:40.580
Forgetting your business cards.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.840
Getting the names of our clients wrong.

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:45.440
And you don't even have a driver's license?

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:47.120
This is ridiculous.

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:47.860
Hm?

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:50.840
I was recruited as a badminton player,

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:54.960
but we only practice in the evenings?
That has to be some kind of bad joke.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:58.160
- At Mitsuhoshi…
- Them's the rules here.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:10:01.180
That's exactly why you'll always be
in the 2nd division.

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:04.420
We actually made a comeback into
the S/J league last year.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.320
But you're in last place.

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:10.160
Sure, compared to Mitsuhoshi,
we've still got a long way to go.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.620
And we're gonna go on that journey together!

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:15.680
I love badminton,
so I'll give my best at practice.

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:18.780
But I'm not planning on being all
buddy-buddy with you.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:23.620
Come on, man. The closer you are
with your partner, the better your results.

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:25.100
Both in badminton, and at work.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:28.000
I wouldn't know. I don't play doubles.

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:31.640
That's a darn shame.

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:32.700
[Matsugishi Elementary School]

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:33.520
[Matsugishi Elementary School]
What…?

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:34.020
[Matsugishi Elementary School]

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:36.840
This is where we practice?

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.100
Gimme a break…

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:40.680
Get out of the way.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:42.540
Toya?

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:44.560
Huh, why are you…?

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:47.420
Don't you think it'd be weirder
if I weren't on the team?

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:49.120
Hey, you!

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:52.640
What's in that big backpack?

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:55.440
Uh, this is…

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:58.780
Why are adults
at an elementary school? Weirdos!

00:10:59.120 --> 00:10:59.940
He's right.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:06.000
I mean, honestly,
practicing at an elementary school gym?

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:07.540
Is that normal?

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:09.640
What, like you're normal?

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:12.080
Who wears that sorta tie
on your first day at work?

00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:14.080
How did you…?!

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:15.740
Hey there!

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:17.800
The Walking Speaker,

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:20.580
[Takeda Koki, 27, SB Sales Dept.]
Takeda Koki makes his entrance.

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:22.440
Oh, it's your fault.

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:26.460
Oh yeah, you should know that
Ko and I play doubles together!

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.650
People call us… Taketo.

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:29.800
Pleasure to meet you.

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:32.360
You're the only one who calls us that!

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:36.440
Hello!

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.340
Hi.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:39.360
Bro, you're early.

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:40.300
Bro?

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:42.960
Oh, right, I guess you never met him.

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:46.460
[Saeki Sota, 23, SB Quality Assurance]
This is my brother, Saeki Sota.
He's four years older than me

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:47.720
[Saeki Sota, 23, SB Quality Assurance]
and plays singles.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:48.960
Nice to meet you.

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:52.840
I'm Shiratori. I also play singles.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:54.560
Oh! You're the butterfly tie guy.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:57.540
Not you again!

00:11:58.160 --> 00:11:59.900
What, it was funny!

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:01.660
Shut yer traps!

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:05.460
Hello, coach!

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:06.760
[Ono Yasuomi, 46,
SB Dir. of General Affairs/Badminton Team Coach]
Hello, coach!

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:08.500
[Ono Yasuomi, 46,
SB Dir. of General Affairs/Badminton Team Coach]

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:09.660
[Ono Yasuomi, 46,
SB Dir. of General Affairs/Badminton Team Coach]
Good to see you, Shiratori.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:10.320
Good to see you, Shiratori.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:11.780
Hope to see you at your best.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:12.500
Yes, sir!

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:16.580
Oh? Is your partner not here yet?

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:19.600
Partner? What do you mean?

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:23.460
What partner could I mean?
Your doubles partner.

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:24.280
Doubles?

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.260
Hey there! Sorry I'm late!

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:32.260
We meet again!

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:36.120
Your partner both in badminton and at work…

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:37.820
…is me!

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:41.600
I'm quitting.
Thank you for everything.

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:43.940
Stop right there, Shiratori!

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:45.740
No one told me I would play doubles!

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:47.820
Of course, I didn't tell you!

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:50.640
- He hadn't told him…?
- So you tricked me?!

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:52.420
- I did and I'm sorry!

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:53.940
- Hey, at least he apologized.
- I did and I'm sorry!

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:57.440
You're much more suited
to doubles than to singles!

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:59.860
My eyes don't lie!

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:02.510
And who the hell are you to decide that?!

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:09.740
I'm going to advance in singles and
prove Mitsuhoshi that they were wrong about me…

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.240
You can do the same thing in doubles, you know?

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:14.560
I don't want to play doubles!

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:16.740
Not to mention,

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:19.600
I wouldn't have come at all if
I knew this team was so damn weak!

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:21.400
Okay, I think you've said enough…

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:22.080
Ko, don't!

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:25.400
I don't want this to be the end for me…

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:30.440
Then hear me out.

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:32.620
Play one-on-one with me.

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:33.500
What?

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:36.020
You don't want to play doubles, right?

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:39.120
So prove that you can beat me in singles.

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:41.040
What are you…?

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:42.000
Sounds good to me.

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:46.200
If you win, I'll let you play singles.

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:52.580
Fine.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:56.540
But in return! If I win, you'll be my partner.

00:13:57.960 --> 00:13:58.800
Fine.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:00.940
But you won't win.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:07.540
One-game match! Shiratori versus Miyazumi.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:09.440
Love all. Play!

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:21.580
Dude…

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:23.460
Tatsu, there!

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:29.500
1-love.

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:40.800
Looks like he can't do squat
when faced with Tatsu's sheer strength.

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:43.480
No, that's Mikoto's playstyle.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.220
So his style is defense?

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:48.280
No. He always observes his opponent first.

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.320
He's watching Tatsuru's movements.

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:52.360
Observes?

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:55.040
7-love.

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:00.300
Got it.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.400
Wait, what just happened?

00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:22.400
That's Shiratori's greatest weapon, Foresight.

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:27.420
The opponent feels like
he can predict their every move.

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:29.600
So he's an Esper…?

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:31.940
So… what exactly does that mean?

00:15:32.020 --> 00:15:36.720
That he's super good at reading people's slightest
movements and guessing what they'll do next.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:41.080
Like how their eyes move, where their body
is facing, and a lot more.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:44.220
From there, he can apparently
predict what they'll do next.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:46.580
No way, that's awesome!

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:56.340
Well, I'll be damned.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.900
He can tell exactly where I'm going to send it.

00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:02.460
But I'm just getting started.

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:06.280
Straight.

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:09.980
He's good.

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:13.480
Going for a cross shot when
it seemed he would hit it straight.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:16.800
11-9.

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:22.080
His Foresight can be a powerful weapon,
but it is also a wager.

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:27.180
Now, doubles is where
Shiratori's skills would really shine.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:32.080
In singles, if he loses that wager,
there's no one who can cover for him.

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:48.820
11-10.

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:53.060
What was that?

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:56.280
He should have been able to hit that, right…?

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:57.860
I knew it…

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:02.180
Come on! Even when my Foresight
gives me the upper hand…!

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:05.360
Oh, get lost!

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:12.820
Heck yeah!

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:16.320
Do you have to go that hard?

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:18.120
Can't you give up already…

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:20.520
Once the shuttlecock falls, you've lost.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:23.620
So I'll make sure it never does.

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:27.580
Why can't you give up
and be my partner already?

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:35.580
The strength to break through enemy's defenses,
and the ability to react to any play.

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:40.160
You'd think he's simple,
but he uses his brain when it matters.

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:41.740
This is rough…!

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:53.180
Right, this ends here, then?

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:54.800
This is just the start.

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:07.900
Dude… When is this rally gonna end?

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:13.540
He's a major pain in the ass as an opponent…

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.870
But, what if…

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:17.740
…he was on my side?

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:22.900
What the hell am I thinking?!

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:41.160
I… I won!

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:45.840
I lost?

00:18:46.380 --> 00:18:47.450
Me, of all people?

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:55.240
Man, singles really sucks the life outta you.

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:57.600
I think I'm dying…

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:02.980
Just don't puke, please.

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:05.360
On that note, spit it out already!

00:19:05.560 --> 00:19:06.220
What?

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:08.780
You like doubles, don't you?

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:11.020
Playing against you made that clear.

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:15.360
Don't talk like you know me.

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:17.540
Well, a deal's a deal.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:20.400
Starting from today, you're my partner.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:26.140
Let's go!

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:31.860
That was one hell of a long day…

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:34.600
We're Miyazumi and Shiratori, so…

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:36.280
MiyaShiro?

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:40.200
No, no, Tatsuru and Mikoto,
so maybe TatsuMiko?

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:42.340
Let's not do the name thing.

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:46.920
What? Would you rather
I put your name first? MikoTatsu?

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:50.780
Just so we're clear,
I still haven't accepted you as my partner!

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:53.170
You lost, so I don't think you get a say here.

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:58.180
Don't sweat it, I'm sure
we'll make great partners!

00:19:58.180 --> 00:19:59.770
Both in badminton and at work!

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:00.860
No way.

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:02.420
Yes way!

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:07.480
I'm going to teach you how fun
the life of a Badryman can be!

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:10.520
What's that lame portmanteau
supposed to mean?

00:20:12.320 --> 00:20:14.280
Why, I'm so glad you asked!

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:16.840
One moment,
we battle in the corporate world,

00:20:17.060 --> 00:20:19.500
the next, on the court!

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:23.820
Superheroes who shape the future
with suits and shuttlecocks…

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:28.540
That's Badrymen!

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.080
Right, good night.

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:33.740
No, wait, don't ignore me!

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:37.840
Honestly, why are you still following me?
Are you stalking me?

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:40.780
What do you mean, "following"?

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:43.200
This is our dorm.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:45.250
[Sunlight Beverage Employee Dorms]

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:46.480
Wha…

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:47.940
[203 Miyazumi, 103 Shiratori]

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:49.400
[203 Miyazumi, 103 Shiratori]
What?!

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:50.940
[203 Miyazumi, 103 Shiratori]

00:22:35.480 --> 00:22:36.660
What's up, li'l guy?

00:22:38.160 --> 00:22:40.120
You should be heading home now, you know.

00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:43.500
Oh, no, don't mind me…

00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:46.060
No, I think I should…

00:22:48.580 --> 00:22:50.040
What's that bag for?

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:52.060
Oh, this?

00:22:52.280 --> 00:22:55.100
It's for this thing called badminton!

00:22:57.440 --> 00:22:59.560
What do you say, wanna give it a shot?

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:01.340
Yeah!

00:23:02.920 --> 00:23:04.700
Who are you, mister?

00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:07.320
Me? I'm…

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:11.440
A superhero who shapes the future
with a suit and shuttlecock…

00:23:11.800 --> 00:23:13.640
A Badryman!
